---
title: Current action flow — acknowledgment is not success
---
sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Current bounded action and its possible outcome
  accDescr: The planner chooses from an observation. The controller checks current authority without refreshing a stale choice. The native bridge validates and dispatches normal input. A ready response means another input boundary, not objective success. A deadline produces uncertainty and frozen remote dispatch; no automatic retry.
  participant P as Codex planner
  participant C as Controller
  participant B as Native bridge
  participant G as CDDA engine
  P->>C: Action + observed session/revision
  C->>B: Observe current input boundary
  B-->>C: Current frame and authority
  Note over C,B: Reject stale choices, pause or invalid input
  C->>B: Valid input + identity + expiry
  B->>G: Normal input at eligible boundary
  alt Next eligible input boundary arrives
    G-->>B: Rendered result or prompt
    B-->>C: ready + new frame and state
    C-->>P: Result to interpret
    Note over P,C: Verify the objective from observation
  else Deadline or transport failure
    C-->>P: Outcome unknown, dispatch frozen
    Note over C,G: Observe to reconcile, never replay blindly
  end
